atem:
  line: A command-line tool and library that statically finds unused code and unreachable code in Python programs
    and reports each finding with a confidence.
  focus: Vulture parses every given Python file, records the names each one defines and uses, and reports the definitions
    whose names are never used, plus code after return, raise, break and continue and branches with constant conditions.
    Each report line follows pyflakes' syntax and carries a confidence from 60% to 100%, and the exit code tells
    whether dead code was found.
  push: Cleaning up large code bases and finding untested code by scanning a library together with its tests.
  pull: The analysis ignores scopes and matches bare names only, so dynamic or implicit uses go unseen and must
    be whitelisted, and some dead code is missed.
