- id: C:behaviour/vulture.lines.get_first_line_number.doc
  type: behaviour
  name: What the docstring of get_first_line_number says
  summary: The docstring of get_first_line_number of vulture.lines, as written.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.lines.get_first_line_number
  when: get_first_line_number is used
  does: 'From Python 3.8 onwards, lineno for decorated objects is the line at which

    the object definition starts, which is different from what Python < 3.8

    reported -- the lineno of the first decorator. To preserve this behaviour

    of Vulture for newer Python versions, which is also more accurate for

    counting the size of the unused code chunk (if the property is unused, we

    also don''t need it''s decorators), we return the lineno of the first

    decorator, if there are any.'
