- id: C:structure/dev.make-release-notes.changelog-section
  type: structure
  name: A changelog release section
  summary: The shape of CHANGELOG.md that dev/make-release-notes.py (the repository's release tooling) reads for
    the newest release.
  stance: observed
  shape: 'A first line "# VERSION (YYYY-MM-DD)" followed by a newline (matched against the pattern ''# VERSION \(\d\d\d\d-\d\d-\d\d\)\n''),
    one empty line, then the notes as lines up to the next empty line. The tool is run as "make-release-notes.py
    VERSION CHANGELOG LIST": it takes the header without its leading "# ", an empty line and the notes; prints them
    between two lines of 60 asterisks; asks ''Accept this changelog (Y/n)? '' (reply stripped and lower-cased; empty
    or "y" accepts, anything else exits with status 1); on acceptance writes them to LIST. A first line not matching
    exits with ''First changelog line "<line>" must start with "<pattern>"''; a non-empty second line exits with
    "There must be an empty line after each header".'
  fields:
  - name: header
    type: line "# <version> (<date>)"
  - name: notes
    type: lines up to the first blank line
  invariants:
  - the header is the very first line of the file
  - exactly one blank line follows the header
  span:
    file: dev/make-release-notes.py
    lines: 6-42
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - dev/make-release-notes.py#L6-L42
    confidence: 0.9
    state: known
  made:
    move: derive
    run: 2026-11-05-2316-661d
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: model:hand-g1c
  ruling:
  - is: free
    because: a Go package's API is the writer's choice
    made-for: N:target/go
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-13'
    said: 'sitting 1, Q10: the Python API free for Go (made-for go); kept for the Python round trip'
  - is: kept
    because: the original's 300 tests call it
    made-for: N:target/python
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-13'
    said: 'sitting 1, Q10: the Python API free for Go (made-for go); kept for the Python round trip'
