- id: C:structure/tests.test-helpers
  type: structure
  name: The test suite's shared helpers
  summary: tests/__init__.py gives the helpers and fixture every test module uses, and so pins what the program
    must expose to them.
  stance: observed
  shape: REPO is the repository root (the parent of tests/). WHITELISTS is the list of paths of every vulture/whitelists/*.py
    file, leaving out pint_whitelist.py on Python 3.13 or later. call_vulture(args, **kwargs) runs "<python> -m
    vulture <args...>" as a subprocess with the repository root as working directory and returns its exit status
    (so the package must be runnable with -m). check(items_or_names, expected_names) asserts that the sorted .name
    of each Item equals the sorted expected names; when the elements have no .name (a set of strings) it asserts
    the set equals set(expected_names). check_unreachable(v, lineno, size, name) asserts that v.unreachable_code
    holds exactly one Item, with that first_lineno, size and name. check_multiple_unreachable(v, checks) asserts
    v.unreachable_code holds one Item per (lineno, size, name) triple, in that order. The fixture v returns a new
    core.Vulture(verbose=True).
  fields:
  - name: Vulture.unreachable_code
    type: a list of Item, in the order found; each has first_lineno, size and name
  - name: Item.name
    type: str
  - name: Item.first_lineno
    type: int
  - name: Item.size
    type: int
  invariants:
  - the unused-code collections a test passes to check are either collections of Item or sets of names (str)
  - Vulture(verbose=True) must be constructible with no other argument
  span:
    file: tests/__init__.py
    lines: 9-54
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - tests/__init__.py#L9-L54
    confidence: 0.9
    state: known
  made:
    move: derive
    run: 2026-11-05-2316-661d
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: model:hand-g1c
  ruling:
  - is: free
    because: a Go package's API is the writer's choice
    made-for: N:target/go
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-13'
    said: 'sitting 1, Q10: the Python API free for Go (made-for go); kept for the Python round trip'
  - is: kept
    because: the original's 300 tests call it
    made-for: N:target/python
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-13'
    said: 'sitting 1, Q10: the Python API free for Go (made-for go); kept for the Python round trip'
