- id: P:case/tests.test_imports.definitions-and-imports-matrix
  type: case
  name: Definitions, imports, aliases and uses
  summary: Each kind of definition is kept in its own list, and a definition is unused when its name is not among
    the used names.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.scan
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.visit_Import
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.visit_ImportFrom
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.unused_classes
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.unused_funcs
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.unused_imports
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.unused_vars
  given:
    input: 'definitions: "class A(object):\n    pass\nclass B(object):\n    pass\ndef C():\n    pass\nD = 42\n"

      imports: "from any_module import A\nimport B, C\nimport D\n"

      aliased_imports: "from any_module import A as AliasA\nimport B as AliasB, C as AliasC\nimport D as AliasD\n"

      uses: "A()\nB()\nC()\nD()\n"

      aliased_uses: "AliasA()\nAliasB()\nAliasC()\nAliasD()\n"

      Every scan defines classes [A, B], funcs [C], vars [D].

      scan(definitions): imports []; used {}; unused classes [A, B], funcs [C], imports [], vars [D]

      scan(definitions + uses): used {A, B, C, D}; nothing unused

      scan(definitions + imports): imports [A, B, C, D]; used {}; unused classes [A, B], funcs [C], imports [A,
      B, C, D], vars [D]

      scan(definitions + imports + uses): imports [A, B, C, D]; used {A, B, C, D}; nothing unused

      scan(definitions + imports + aliased_uses): used {AliasA, AliasB, AliasC, AliasD}; unused classes [A, B],
      funcs [C], imports [A, B, C, D], vars [D]

      scan(definitions + aliased_imports): imports [AliasA, AliasB, AliasC, AliasD]; used {A, B, C, D}; unused imports
      [AliasA, AliasB, AliasC, AliasD] only

      scan(definitions + aliased_imports + uses): the same as the line before

      scan(definitions + aliased_imports + aliased_uses): used {A, B, C, D, AliasA, AliasB, AliasC, AliasD}; nothing
      unused'
  expect:
    value: v.defined_classes, defined_funcs, defined_imports, defined_vars (lists of Item, compared by sorted names),
      v.used_names (a set) and the unused_* properties as listed for each scan
  span:
    file: tests/test_imports.py
    lines: 68-209
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - tests/test_imports.py#L68-L209
    confidence: 0.9
