- id: P:case/tests.test_make_whitelist.whitelist-round-trip
  type: case
  name: Scanning each item's whitelist string makes it used
  summary: After scanning code, scanning item.get_whitelist_string() for every unused item (with the same Vulture)
    leaves no unused code, except unreachable code.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Item.get_whitelist_string
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.get_unused_code
  given:
    calls:
    - v = Vulture(verbose=True); v.scan(code); names of v.get_unused_code() == before
    - 'for item in v.get_unused_code(): v.scan(item.get_whitelist_string())'
    - names of v.get_unused_code() == after
    input: 'code -> before -> after

      "def func():\n    pass\n" -> [func] -> []

      "class Foo:\n    def __init__(self):\n        pass\n" -> [Foo] -> []

      "foo = ''unused''\nbar = ''variable''\n" -> [foo, bar] -> []

      "import xyz\nimport foo as bar\nfrom abc import iou\nfrom lorem import ipsum as dolor\n" -> [xyz, bar, iou,
      dolor] -> []

      "class Foo:\n    def bar(self):\n        self.foobar = ''unused attr''\n" -> [Foo, bar, foobar] -> []

      "class Foo:\n    @property\n    def bar(self):\n        pass\n" -> [Foo, bar] -> []

      "def foo():\n    return \"Foo Bar\"\n    print(\"Hello\")\n" -> [foo, return] -> [return]'
  expect:
    value: the after list for each code; an unreachable-code item (named "return") stays reported after its whitelist
      string is scanned
  span:
    file: tests/test_make_whitelist.py
    lines: 9-80
