- id: P:case/tests.test_reachability.unreachable-after-flow-ends
  type: case
  name: Statements after return, raise, continue and break
  summary: The statements after a return, raise, continue or break in the same block are one unreachable item named
    after that statement; first_lineno is the first such statement's line and size runs to the last line of the
    block's last statement, comments between included.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.reachability.Reachability.visit
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.scan
  given:
    calls:
    - v = Vulture(verbose=True); v.scan(code); then v.unreachable_code must hold exactly the (first_lineno, size,
      name) given
    input: '"def foo():\n    print(\"Hello World\")\n    return\n    a = 1\n" -> (4, 1, return)

      "def foo():\n    print(\"Something\")\n    return (something,\n            that,\n            spans,\n            over,\n            multiple,\n            lines)\n    print(\"Hello
      World\")\n" -> (9, 1, return)

      "def foo():\n    return something\n    return None\n    return (some, statement)\n" -> (3, 2, return)

      "def foo():\n    return\n    pass\n    return something\n" -> (3, 2, return)

      "\ndef foo():\n    return \\\n        \"Hello\"\n    print(\"Unreachable code\")\n" -> (4, 1, return)   (the
      code starts with an empty line; the return is continued with a backslash)

      "def foo(a):\n    if a == 1:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        return foo(a - 1)\n        print(\"This
      line is never executed\")\n" -> (6, 1, return)

      "def foo():\n    return; a = 1\n" -> (2, 1, return)

      "def foo(a):\n    return\n    a[1:2]\n" -> (3, 1, return)

      "def foo():\n    if foo():\n        return True\n        continue\n    else:\n        return False\n" -> (4,
      1, return)

      "def foo():\n    return True\n    def bar():\n        return False\n" -> (3, 2, return)

      "raise ValueError\na = 1\n" -> (2, 1, raise)   (at module level)

      "def foo():\n    raise ValueError\n    li = []\n" -> (3, 1, raise)

      "def foo():\n    a = 1\n    raise\n    raise KeyError\n    # a comment\n    b = 2\n    raise CustomDefinedError\n"
      -> (4, 4, raise)

      "def foo():\n    a = 1\n    return\n    raise ValueError\n    return\n" -> (4, 2, return)

      "def foo():\n    return\n    # This is a comment\n    print(\"Hello World\")\n" -> (4, 1, return)

      "def foo():\n    a = 1\n    raise\n    return a\n" -> (4, 1, raise)

      "def foo():\n    raise SomeError(\"There is a problem\")\n    print(\"I am unreachable\")\n" -> (3, 1, raise)

      "def foo():\n    try:\n        a = 1\n        raise\n    except IOError as e:\n        print(\"We have some
      problem.\")\n        raise\n        print(\":-(\")\n" -> (8, 1, raise)

      "def foo():\n    raise\n    # This is a comment\n    print(\"Something\")\n    return None\n" -> (4, 2, raise)

      "def foo():\n    if bar():\n        a = 1\n    else:\n        continue\n        a = 2\n" -> (6, 1, continue)   (continue
      outside a loop must still be scanned: the code is parsed, never compiled)

      "def foo():\n    a = 0\n    if something():\n        foo()\n        if bar():\n            a = 2\n            continue\n            #
      This is unreachable\n            a = 1\n        elif a == 1:\n            pass\n        else:\n            a
      = 3\n            continue\n    else:\n        continue\n" -> (9, 1, continue)

      "def foo():\n    if bar1():\n        bar2()\n    else:\n        a = 1\n        continue\n        # Just a
      comment\n        raise ValueError\n" -> (8, 1, continue)

      "def foo():\n    for i in range(123):\n        break\n        # A comment\n        return\n        dead =
      1\n" -> (5, 2, break)

      "while True:\n    break\n    # some comment\n    print(\"Hello\")\n" -> (4, 1, break)'
  expect:
    value: exactly one item in v.unreachable_code, with the first_lineno, size and name given for each code
  span:
    file: tests/test_reachability.py
    lines: 6-346
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - tests/test_reachability.py#L6-L346
    confidence: 0.9
    state: known
  made:
    move: derive
    run: 2026-11-05-2316-661d
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: model:hand-g1c
  stands: inside
  from: test
