- id: P:case/tests.test_reachability.unreachable-conditions
  type: case
  name: Branches a constant condition never takes
  summary: An if or elif whose condition is always false is an item "if" from its test line to the end of its own
    body; when the condition is always true, the else branch is an item "else" from its first statement to its end;
    an always-true if with no else is itself reported as a redundant "if"; a conditional expression with a constant
    test is an item "ternary".
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.reachability.Reachability.visit
  - C:interface/vulture.utils.condition_is_always_false
  - C:interface/vulture.utils.condition_is_always_true
  given:
    input: '"if False:\n    pass\n" -> (1, 2, if)

      "if bar():\n    pass\nelif False:\n    print(\"Unreachable\")\n" -> (3, 2, if)

      "if foo():\n    if bar():\n        pass\n    elif False:\n        print(\"Unreachable\")\n        pass\n    elif
      something():\n        print(\"Reachable\")\n    else:\n        pass\nelse:\n    pass\n" -> (4, 3, if)

      "if False: a = 1\nelse: c = 3\n" -> (1, 1, if)

      "if True:\n    a = 1\n    b = 2\nelse:\n    c = 3\n    d = 3\n" -> (5, 2, else)   (the else line itself is
      not reported, for simplicity)

      "if True:\n    a = 1\n    b = 2\nelse: c = 3\nd = 3\n" -> (4, 1, else)

      "if foo():\n    if bar():\n        pass\n    elif True:\n        if something():\n            pass\n        else:\n            pass\n    elif
      something_else():\n        print(\"foo\")\n    else:\n        print(\"bar\")\nelse:\n    pass\n" -> (9, 4,
      else)   (the elif chain after "elif True" from its line 9 to line 12)

      "if [5]:\n    pass\n" -> (1, 2, if)

