- id: P:case/tests.test_scavenging.methods
  type: case
  name: Methods are kept apart from functions and matched by name only
  summary: A def inside a class is a method (defined_methods), async too; a method is used when its name is used
    anywhere, so a module function of the same name being called hides an unused method; classmethods and staticmethods
    are reported when unused.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.visit_FunctionDef
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.unused_methods
  given:
    input: '"class Foo:\n    async def bar(self):\n        pass\n" -> classes [Foo]; funcs []; methods [bar]; unused
      classes [Foo]; unused methods [bar]

      "class Bar(object):\n    def func(self):\n        pass\n\ndef func():\n    pass\n\nfunc()\n" -> classes [Bar];
      funcs [func]; methods [func]; unused classes [Bar]; unused funcs []; unused methods []  (Bar.func is unused
      but not detected, to avoid a false positive in the next case)

      "class Bar(object):\n    def func(self):\n        pass\n\n    other_name_for_func = func\n\nBar().other_name_for_func()\n"
      -> classes [Bar]; funcs []; methods [func]; vars [other_name_for_func]; nothing unused

      "class Bar(object):\n    def foo(self):\n        pass\n\nb = Bar()\nb.foo\n" -> used_names {Bar, b, foo};
      classes [Bar]; funcs []; methods [foo]; unused classes [] and funcs []

      "def __init__(self):\n    self.a.foo()\n\nclass Bar(object):\n    def foo(self):\n        pass\n\n    @classmethod\n    def
      bar(cls):\n        pass\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def foobar():\n        pass\n" -> classes [Bar]; funcs []
      (a dunder function is not defined); methods [foo, bar, foobar]; unused classes [Bar]; unused funcs []; unused
      methods [bar, foobar]'
