- id: C:behaviour/vulture.config.check-input-config
  type: behaviour
  name: Checking configuration keys and value types
  summary: _check_input_config refuses an unknown key or a value whose type is not exactly the type of the key's
    default.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.config._check_input_config
  when: _check_input_config(data) is called with a dict (from the TOML table or the command line)
  does: 'For each (key, value) in data, in order: if key is not a key of DEFAULTS, raises InputError("Unknown configuration
    key: <key>"). Otherwise compares type(value) with type(DEFAULTS[key]) by identity (not isinstance, so that bool
    and int are told apart); if they differ, raises InputError("Data type for <key> must be ''<typename>''") where
    typename is the default''s type name quoted with repr, e.g. ''list'', ''bool'', ''int'', ''str''. Returns None
    when every entry passes.'
  edges:
  - given: '{"min_confidence": True}'
    then: 'InputError: Data type for min_confidence must be ''int'''
  - given: '{"verbose": 0}'
    then: 'InputError: Data type for verbose must be ''bool'''
  - given: '{}'
    then: passes
  errors:
  - when: a key not in DEFAULTS
    message: 'Unknown configuration key: {key}'
    exit: (raised; the command line turns it into exit code InvalidInput)
  - when: a value of another type than the default
    message: Data type for {key} must be {expected_type!r}
    exit: (raised)
  span:
    file: vulture/config.py
    lines: 35-47
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - vulture/config.py#L35-L47
    confidence: 0.9
    state: known
  made:
    move: derive
    run: 2026-11-05-2316-661d
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: model:hand-g1c
  ruling:
  - is: kept
    because: the words are output text
    by: R:maker/transconceiver
    'on': '2026-11-13'
    said: '5d Q-D1: ruled as proposed, in one batch: every pending item takes the worksheet''s proposal (sections
      1 and 2''s last column); the owner may overrule any one later'
    about: V-R09
  - is: kept
    about: the rest of the behaviour
