- id: C:behaviour/vulture.config.parse-args
  type: behaviour
  name: Reading the command line
  summary: _parse_args reads the command line with the option reader of V-R03 and returns only the options actually
    given (plus config).
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.config._parse_args
  - C:interface/command.vulture
  when: _parse_args(args) is called; args None means sys.argv[1:]
  does: 'Builds a parser with prog "vulture" and usage "%(prog)s [options] [PATH ...]" (shown as "vulture [options]
    [PATH ...]"). Arguments, in this order: paths (nargs *, metavar PATH); --exclude, --ignore-decorators and --ignore-names
    (metavar PATTERNS, each value split at every comma into a list of strings with a local helper csv(exclude) =
    exclude.split(","), nothing stripped); --make-whitelist (store_true); --min-confidence (int); --sort-by-size
    (store_true); --config (str, default "pyproject.toml"); -v/--verbose (store_true); --version (prints "vulture
    <__version__>" and exits 0). Every option except --config defaults to a private sentinel object (missing) so
    that an option not given can be told from one given as False; after parsing, every entry still equal to the
    sentinel is dropped, so the dict holds config plus only what was given (paths is absent when no path is given,
    since a positional with nargs * takes its default, the sentinel, when empty). The dict is checked with _check_input_config
    and returned. Help texts: paths "Paths may be Python files or directories. For each directory Vulture analyzes
    all contained *.py files."; --exclude ''Comma-separated list of path patterns to ignore (e.g., "*settings.py,docs,*/test_*.py,venv").
    Patterns may contain glob wildcards (*, ?, [abc], [!abc]). A PATTERN without glob wildcards is treated as *PATTERN*.
    Patterns are matched against absolute paths.''; --ignore-decorators ''Comma-separated list of decorators. Functions
    and classes using these decorators are ignored (e.g., "@app.route,@require_*"). Patterns may contain glob wildcards
    (*, ?, [abc], [!abc]).''; --ignore-names ''Comma-separated list of names to ignore (e.g., "visit_*,do_*"). Patterns
    may contain glob wildcards (*, ?, [abc], [!abc]).''; --make-whitelist "Report unused code in a format that can
    be added to a whitelist module."; --min-confidence "Minimum confidence (between 0 and 100) for code to be reported
    as unused."; --sort-by-size "Sort unused functions and classes by their lines of code."; --config "Path to pyproject.toml
    config file."; --verbose has no help text.'
  edges:
  - given: '["--exclude=file*.py,dir/", "path1"]'
    then: '{"paths": ["path1"], "exclude": ["file*.py", "dir/"], "config": "pyproject.toml"}'
  - given: '["--version"]'
    then: prints "vulture <version>" to standard output and exits with status 0 (SystemExit)
  - given: an unknown option such as --invalid-argument
    then: argparse prints its usage and error to standard error and exits with status 2 (SystemExit)
  errors:
  - when: --min-confidence is not an integer
    message: 'argparse: "argument --min-confidence: invalid int value: ''<v>''"'
    exit: '2'
  span:
    file: vulture/config.py
    lines: 93-183
