- id: C:behaviour/vulture.core.item-record
  type: behaviour
  name: An item of unused code
  summary: Item holds one finding (name, kind, file, lines, message, confidence) and compares by file, first line
    and name.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Item
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Item.__init__
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Item.__repr__
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Item.__eq__
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Item.__hash__
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Item.size
  when: an Item is made by Vulture._define, or compared, hashed, printed
  does: 'Item(name, typ, filename, first_lineno, last_lineno, message="", confidence=DEFAULT_CONFIDENCE) stores
    the seven fields (__slots__ only: confidence, filename, first_lineno, last_lineno, message, name, typ). filename
    is a pathlib.Path. When message is empty it becomes "unused <typ> ''<name>''" (e.g. "unused function ''foo''").
    typ is one of attribute, class, function, import, method, property, variable, unreachable_code. size is last_lineno
    - first_lineno + 1 (it asserts last_lineno >= first_lineno). repr(item) is repr(item.name), e.g. ''foo'' with
    quotes. Equality and hash use the tuple (filename, first_lineno, name) through the private helper _tuple(self),
    so two definitions of one name on one line of one file are one item.'
  edges:
  - given: Item("foo", "function", Path("a.py"), 3, 5)
    then: message "unused function 'foo'", confidence 60, size 3
