- id: C:behaviour/vulture.core.scan-code
  type: behaviour
  name: Scanning one module's source
  summary: scan parses a source string, collects its noqa comments, visits its tree to record definitions and uses,
    and records invalid input in exit_code.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.scan
  when: scan(code, filename="") is called with the source text of one module
  does: '1. filename becomes Path(filename) (an empty name is Path(".")); self.code becomes code.splitlines(); self.noqa_lines
    becomes noqa.parse_noqa(self.code); self.filename is set (items made during this scan carry it). 2. Parses with
    ast.parse(code, filename=str(filename), type_comments=True): the code is parsed, never compiled, so a continue
    outside a loop is accepted; type comments are parsed too. 3. On SyntaxError: prints to standard error, always
    (forced), "<format_path(filename)>:<lineno>: <msg>" plus '' at "<the offending text, stripped>"'' when the error
    carries text, and sets exit_code to InvalidInput. On ValueError (the source holds a null byte): prints ''<format_path(filename)>:
    invalid source code "<error>"'' to standard error and sets exit_code to InvalidInput. Nothing is defined from
    that module. 4. Otherwise visits the tree (self.visit); a SyntaxError raised while visiting (an invalid type
    comment) is handled as in 3. 5. Finally resets the reachability analyser (reachability.reset()) to free memory.
    scan returns None and never raises for bad input.'
  edges:
  - given: '"foo bar"'
    then: 'stderr ".:1: invalid syntax at \"foo bar\"" (the message is Python''s own); exit_code InvalidInput'
  - given: '"\x00"'
    then: exit_code InvalidInput
  - given: 'a function whose type comment is "# type: bogus"'
    then: exit_code InvalidInput
  errors:
  - when: the code does not parse
    message: '<path>:<lineno>: <msg> at "<text>"'
    exit: exit_code InvalidInput (no exception)
  - when: the code holds a null byte
    message: '<path>: invalid source code "<error>"'
    exit: exit_code InvalidInput
  span:
    file: vulture/core.py
