- id: C:behaviour/vulture.core.scavenge-paths
  type: behaviour
  name: Scanning files and folders, then the bundled whitelists
  summary: scavenge scans every Python module under the given paths that no exclude pattern matches, then scans
    the bundled whitelist of every imported module that has one.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.scavenge
  when: scavenge(paths, exclude=None) is called (by main with the configured paths and exclude list)
  does: '1. Exclude patterns: empty patterns are dropped (an empty pattern would match everything); a pattern holding
    none of the characters *, ? or [ becomes *pattern*. A path is excluded when it matches any pattern with fnmatch.fnmatch
    (case-insensitive on every platform here, since the private helper _match(name, patterns, case=False) is used;
    * also matches "/"). 2. Every path is made a pathlib.Path; utils.get_modules(paths) gives the modules to read,
    in its order. For each: if excluded, logs "Excluded: <module>" (verbose only) and skips it; else logs "Scanning:
    <module>", reads it with utils.read_file; when that raises utils.VultureInputException, prints to standard error
    (forced) "Error: Could not read file <module> - <error>" and on the next line "Try to change the encoding to
    UTF-8." and sets exit_code to InvalidInput; otherwise scans the text with the module''s path as filename. 3.
    Then for every distinct name among defined_imports (in no fixed order) takes the relative path whitelists/<name>_whitelist.py.
    If an exclude pattern matches it, logs "Excluded whitelist: <path>". Otherwise reads it as package data of vulture
    (pkgutil.get_data("vulture", path)); when there is no such file (OSError) it moves on silently; else logs "Included
    whitelist: <path>", decodes it as UTF-8 and scans it with that relative path as filename. So importing argparse,
    ast, collections, ctypes, enum, logging, socketserver, ssl, string, sys, threading, unittest or pint brings
    in the names vulture''s whitelist for that module uses.'
  edges:
  - given: exclude ["", "no_match"] and a file holding "import os"
    then: the file is scanned; unused code is [os]
  - given: exclude ["whitelists"]
    then: 'becomes *whitelists*: every bundled whitelist and any path containing "whitelists" is skipped'
  - given: a file in UTF-16
    then: the read fails; exit_code InvalidInput; the other files are still scanned
  errors:
  - when: a module cannot be read or decoded
    message: 'Error: Could not read file <module> - <error>

      Try to change the encoding to UTF-8.'
    exit: exit_code InvalidInput
  span:
    file: vulture/core.py
    lines: 267-316
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - vulture/core.py#L267-L316
    confidence: 0.9
