- id: C:behaviour/vulture.core.get-unused-code
  type: behaviour
  name: Collecting and ordering the unused code
  summary: get_unused_code gathers the unused items of every kind, keeps those at or above the minimum confidence,
    and sorts them by file and line or by size.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.get_unused_code
  when: get_unused_code(min_confidence=0, sort_by_size=False) is called
  does: 'Raises ValueError("min_confidence must be between 0 and 100.") when min_confidence is below 0 or above
    100. Concatenates, in this order, unused_attrs, unused_classes, unused_funcs, unused_imports, unused_methods,
    unused_props, unused_vars and unreachable_code (all of it: unreachable code is always "unused"). Keeps the items
    whose confidence >= min_confidence. Sorts stably by (str(filename).lower(), first_lineno), or with sort_by_size
    by (size, str(filename).lower(), first_lineno); items equal on the key keep the concatenation order. Returns
    a new list of Item.'
  edges:
  - given: min_confidence 150
    then: 'ValueError: min_confidence must be between 0 and 100.'
  - given: min_confidence equal to an item's confidence
    then: the item is kept
  - given: foo of 3 lines then bar of 2 lines, sort_by_size
    then: '[bar, foo]'
  errors:
  - when: min_confidence outside 0..100
    message: min_confidence must be between 0 and 100.
    exit: (ValueError raised)
