- id: C:behaviour/vulture.core.ignore-rules
  type: behaviour
  name: The kind-specific ignore rules
  summary: Private rules drop imports in __init__.py and star imports, pytest hooks and test functions and Test
    classes in test files, dunder methods, and variables named self, object, _x or __x__.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.visit_ClassDef
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.visit_FunctionDef
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.visit_arg
  when: _define consults the ignore function of the definition's kind
  does: '_is_test_file(filename): filename.resolve() (an absolute path) matches, case-insensitively, one of "*/test/*",
    "*/tests/*", "*/test*.py", "*[-_]test.py". _is_special_name(name): starts and ends with "__". _ignore_class(filename,
    class_name): a test file and "Test" occurs in the class name (case-sensitive). _ignore_import(filename, import_name):
    the file''s name is __init__.py, or the name is "*". _ignore_function(filename, function_name): the name is
    one of PYTEST_FUNCTION_NAMES or starts with "test_", and the file is a test file. _ignore_method(filename, method_name):
    a special (dunder) name anywhere, or (one of PYTEST_METHOD_NAMES or starting with "test_") in a test file. _ignore_variable(filename,
    varname): the name is in IGNORED_VARIABLE_NAMES ("object", "self"), or starts with "_" but not "__" (so _, _a,
    _d_), or is special (__c__); __b is kept. Properties and attributes have no ignore function.'
  edges:
  - given: class BasicTestCase in dir/test_function_names.py
    then: ignored
  - given: def test_func in dir/function_names.py
    then: reported (not a test file)
  - given: variable __b
    then: reported
