- id: C:behaviour/vulture.core.classes-and-functions
  type: behaviour
  name: Defining classes, functions, methods and properties
  summary: A class or def is defined in the collection its decorators and first argument choose, unless a decorator
    matches --ignore-decorators.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.visit_ClassDef
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.visit_FunctionDef
  - C:interface/vulture.core.Vulture.visit_AsyncFunctionDef
  when: the visitor meets a ClassDef, FunctionDef or AsyncFunctionDef (the async one is handled exactly as a def)
  does: 'Class: if any decorator''s name (utils.get_decorator_name, e.g. "@dataclass") matches an ignore_decorators
    pattern (case-sensitive glob), logs ''Ignoring class "<name>" (decorator whitelisted)'' and defines nothing;
    else defines a class (confidence 60, the test-class ignore rule). Function: computes all decorator names; its
    kind is "property" when "@property" is among them; else "method" when "@staticmethod" or "@classmethod" is among
    them or its first positional argument is named self (whether or not it is inside a class: a module-level def
    f(self) is a method, and a def inside a class without self is a function); else "function". If any decorator
    name matches an ignore_decorators pattern, logs ''Ignoring <kind> "<name>" (decorator whitelisted)'' and defines
    nothing; else defines a property (no ignore rule), a method (method rule) or a function (function rule), all
    with confidence 60. Arguments, bodies and decorators are visited afterwards by the generic visit.'
  edges:
  - given: '@property @bar def foo with ignore_decorators ["@b*r"]'
    then: not defined
  - given: 'class Foo: async def bar(self)'
    then: a method bar
  - given: def __init__(self) at module level
    then: a method, ignored as a special name
  - given: '@a.b.c with pattern "@a.b"'
    then: not matched (the whole name must match)
  span:
    file: vulture/core.py
    lines: 553-599
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - vulture/core.py#L553-L599
    confidence: 0.9
