- id: C:behaviour/vulture.core.main
  type: behaviour
  name: The command line
  summary: main builds the configuration, scans the paths and exits with the report's exit code.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.core.main
  - C:component/vulture.core
  when: main() is called (by python -m vulture or the vulture console script)
  does: '1. config = make_config() (reads sys.argv and pyproject.toml). An InputError is printed to standard error
    (its message, e.g. "Please pass at least one file or directory") and the process exits with ExitCode.InvalidCmdlineArguments.
    argparse''s own errors (an unknown option, a bad int) exit inside make_config with argparse''s status 2; --help
    and --version exit 0 there. 2. Makes Vulture(verbose, ignore_names, ignore_decorators) from the config. 3. scavenge(paths,
    exclude). 4. Exits the process with report(min_confidence, sort_by_size, make_whitelist): DeadCode when anything
    was reported, InvalidInput when a file could not be read or parsed and nothing was reported, NoDeadCode otherwise.'
  edges:
