- id: C:behaviour/vulture.reachability.reachability-visit
  type: behaviour
  name: Deciding which nodes end the flow
  summary: Reachability.visit is called for every node after its children and marks the nodes after which control
    cannot continue, reporting unreachable code as it goes.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.reachability.Reachability
  - C:interface/vulture.reachability.Reachability.__init__
  - C:interface/vulture.reachability.Reachability.visit
  - C:interface/vulture.reachability.Reachability.reset
  - C:component/vulture.reachability
  when: Vulture.visit calls reachability.visit(node) for every node, children first (post-order); reset() is called
    after each module
  does: 'Reachability(report) keeps report (a function called with name, first_node, last_node (optional) and message;
    Vulture''s defines an unreachable_code item with confidence 100) and an empty set of nodes that cannot fall
    through (private _mark_as_no_fall_through(node) adds one; _can_fall_through(node) is "not in the set"). reset()
    empties the set. visit(node): Break, Continue, Return and Raise are marked as not falling through. Module, FunctionDef,
    AsyncFunctionDef, With and AsyncWith: their body is analysed with the private _can_fall_through_statements_analysis(statements)
    (the result is not used: these nodes are never marked, so a with whose body always raises still falls through).
    While: _handle_reachability_while. For and AsyncFor: the body is analysed, the loop is never marked (it may
    run zero times). If: _handle_reachability_if. IfExp: _handle_reachability_if_expr. Try: _handle_reachability_try.
    Any other node does nothing (in particular a class body is never analysed, and a match statement is not).'
  edges:
  - given: a with block whose body raises, then a statement
    then: nothing reported
  - given: a for loop whose body raises, then a statement
    then: nothing reported
  span:
    file: vulture/reachability.py
    lines: 6-45
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - vulture/reachability.py#L6-L45
    confidence: 0.9
    state: known
