- id: C:behaviour/vulture.reachability.statements-analysis
  type: behaviour
  name: Unreachable statements in a block
  summary: In a list of statements, everything after the first statement that cannot fall through is one unreachable
    item.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.reachability.Reachability.visit
  when: the private _can_fall_through_statements_analysis(self, statements) is called on a block
  does: 'Walks the statements in order. At the first one marked as not falling through: if more statements follow,
    reports one item named after that statement''s node class in lower case ("return", "raise", "continue", "break",
    "if", "while", "try"), from the next statement (first_node) to the block''s last statement (last_node), with
    message "unreachable code after ''<name>''"; then returns False. Returns True when no statement stops the flow.
    Only the first stopping statement counts: the later statements form a single item.'
  edges:
  - given: "return\n    pass\n    return something"
    then: one item from the pass to the last return, named return, 'unreachable code after ''return'''
  - given: a stopping statement that is the last of its block
    then: nothing reported; returns False
  span:
