  type: behaviour
  name: while loops with constant tests
  summary: while False is reported whole; while True reports its else and, with no break of its own, stops the flow.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.reachability.Reachability.visit
  when: the private _handle_reachability_while(self, node) runs for a While
  does: 'Always false: reports name "while" from the While to its last body statement, message "unsatisfiable ''while''
    condition". Always true: when there is an else, reports name "else" over the else block, message "unreachable
    ''else'' block"; and when the body has no break of this loop (private static _body_has_break(stmts)), marks
    the While as not falling through. In every case the body is then analysed for unreachable statements. A while
    with an else and an undecidable test does not analyse its else. _body_has_break(stmts): True when a statement
    is a Break; nested While, For, AsyncFor, FunctionDef, AsyncFunctionDef and ClassDef are skipped (their breaks
    do not leave this loop); for any other statement it looks recursively into every list field of AST nodes (if/else
    bodies, try bodies, handlers, with bodies...).'
  edges:
  - given: "while True:\n    raise Exception()\nprint(\":-(\")"
    then: (3, 1, while) unreachable code after 'while'
  - given: "while True:\n    for _ in range(3):\n        break\n    while False:\n        break\nprint(\":-(\")"
    then: '[(4, 2, while), (6, 1, while)]'
  - given: "while True:\n    if a > 3:\n        raise Exception()\n    else:\n        break\nprint(\":-(\")"
    then: nothing
  - given: "while a > 0:\n    return 1\nprint(1)"
    then: nothing (the loop may not run)
  span:
    file: vulture/reachability.py
    lines: 137-192
  provenance:
    mode: derived
