- id: C:behaviour/vulture.utils.decorator-name
  type: behaviour
  name: Naming a decorator
  summary: get_decorator_name gives "@" and the dotted name of a decorator, dropping a trailing call.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.utils.get_decorator_name
  when: get_decorator_name(decorator) is called with a decorator expression
  does: When the decorator is a call, takes the called expression. Then collects attribute names while the node
    is an Attribute, going to its value, and finally the id of the Name reached; returns "@" + the parts joined
    by "." in source order. When the chain ends in something without an id (a call, a subscript...), the parts are
    discarded and the result is "@" alone.
  edges:
  - given: '@foo.bar.route(''/foobar'')'
    then: '"@foo.bar.route"'
  - given: '@z.func("hi").bar().k.foo'
    then: '"@"'
  - given: '@foo[2]'
    then: '"@"'
