- id: C:behaviour/vulture.utils.get-modules
  type: behaviour
  name: Finding the files to scan
  summary: get_modules turns the given paths into the list of files to scan, exiting on a missing path or a .pyc
    file.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.utils.get_modules
  when: get_modules(paths) is called with pathlib.Path objects (by Vulture.scavenge)
  does: 'For each path in order, resolves it to an absolute path. A file ending in .pyc stops the program with sys.exit("Error:
    *.pyc files are not supported: <path>") (the message goes to standard error, status 1); any other file is taken
    as given, whatever its suffix; a directory adds every *.py file below it, recursively (Path.rglob, in the file
    system''s order, not sorted); a path that does not exist stops the program with sys.exit("Error: <path> could
    not be found.") (status 1, which equals ExitCode.InvalidInput). Returns the list of absolute paths (so exclude
    patterns are matched against absolute paths).'
  edges:
  - given: missing.py
    then: 'stderr "Error: <cwd>/missing.py could not be found."; exit 1'
  - given: missing.pyc (does not exist)
    then: the same "could not be found" error; exit 1
  errors:
  - when: an existing .pyc file is given
    message: 'Error: *.pyc files are not supported: {path}'
    exit: 1
  - when: a path does not exist
    message: 'Error: {path} could not be found.'
    exit: 1
  span:
    file: vulture/utils.py
    lines: 82-102
  provenance:
    mode: derived
