- id: C:behaviour/vulture.utils.read-file
  type: behaviour
  name: Reading a source file
  summary: read_file reads a file with the encoding its coding cookie or byte-order mark declares, UTF-8 otherwise.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/vulture.utils.read_file
  when: read_file(filename) is called for each module
  does: Opens the file with tokenize.open (which detects a PEP 263 coding cookie or a UTF-8 byte-order mark, strips
    the BOM, and defaults to UTF-8) and returns its text. A SyntaxError (an unknown or conflicting encoding declaration)
    or UnicodeDecodeError is re-raised as VultureInputException chained from the original error. Other OSErrors
    propagate.
  edges:
  - given: a file holding only the UTF-8 BOM
    then: '""'
  - given: a file starting with the UTF-16 LE BOM
    then: VultureInputException
  errors:
  - when: the file cannot be decoded
    message: '(VultureInputException; the caller prints "Error: Could not read file ...")'
    exit: '-'
  span:
