- id: C:behaviour/vulture.whitelists.ast_whitelist.ast-whitelist
  type: behaviour
  name: The ast whitelist
  summary: vulture's bundled whitelist for ast uses every ast.NodeVisitor visit_<Node> method name, because NodeVisitor
    calls them implicitly.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:component/vulture.whitelists.ast_whitelist
  when: a scanned module imports ast (scavenge then scans whitelists/ast_whitelist.py)
  does: 'The file imports Whitelist from whitelist_utils (the sibling module vulture/whitelists/whitelist_utils.py,
    found

    when the file is run from its own folder), makes whitelist_node_visitor = Whitelist() under the comment

    "# NodeVisitor methods are called implicitly.", and then has one line "whitelist_node_visitor.<name>" for each

    of these names, in this order:

    visit_Assert visit_Assign visit_AsyncFor visit_AsyncFunctionDef visit_AsyncWith visit_Attribute

    visit_AugAssign visit_Await visit_BinOp visit_BoolOp visit_Bytes visit_Call visit_ClassDef visit_Compare

    visit_Constant visit_Delete visit_Dict visit_DictComp visit_ExceptHandler visit_Exec visit_Expr

    visit_Expression visit_ExtSlice visit_For visit_FunctionDef visit_GeneratorExp visit_Global visit_If

    visit_IfExp visit_Import visit_ImportFrom visit_Index visit_Interactive visit_Lambda visit_List visit_ListComp

    visit_MatchClass visit_Module visit_Name visit_NameConstant visit_Nonlocal visit_Num visit_Print visit_Raise

    visit_Repr visit_Return visit_Set visit_SetComp visit_Slice visit_Starred visit_Str visit_Subscript

    visit_Suite visit_Try visit_TryExcept visit_TryFinally visit_Tuple visit_UnaryOp visit_While visit_With

    visit_Yield visit_YieldFrom visit_alias visit_arg visit_arguments visit_comprehension visit_keyword

    (67 lines, lines 6-72). Each line reads an attribute of a Whitelist object, which accepts any attribute name.'
  span:
    file: vulture/whitelists/ast_whitelist.py
    lines: 1-72
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
