- id: N:decision/names-not-scopes
  type: decision
  name: Match names, ignore scopes
  summary: Vulture records defined and used names and ignores scopes, so any use of a name anywhere marks every
    definition of it used.
  stance: observed
  chose: name-only matching across all scanned files
  over:
  - option: scope-aware analysis
    because:
      pending: 'why was scope analysis not attempted: cost, complexity, or the dynamic nature of Python?'
  because: It is simple and fast, at the price of false negatives (a used name hides an unused definition of the
    same name elsewhere).
  span:
    file: README.md
