- id: N:target/go
  type: target
  name: go
  summary: vulture weighed for a transconception into Go; feasible with named gaps (the grammar written, TOML and
    NFKC from pinned modules, the option reader written).
  stance: observed
  language: go
  version: 1.27.4
  program: vulture
  weighed:
  - point: 1
    score: 2
    evidence: one company leads (Google); published proposal process; releases since 1.0 in 2012; BSD licence; a
      second compiler, gccgo
  - point: 2
    score: 3
    evidence: The Go Programming Language Specification (CC BY 4.0); gc and gccgo
  - point: 3
    score: 3
    evidence: the Go 1 compatibility promise; the go line and GODEBUG since 1.21
  - point: 4
    score: 2
    evidence: 'every kept reliance provided: 11 built-in, 3 library, 18 written, 1 dropped (free), none cannot;
      the grammar is written'
  - point: 5
    score: 3
    evidence: one static program with CGO_ENABLED=0 on macOS arm64, Linux, Windows
  - point: 6
    score: 3
    evidence: a tree walked children first, sets and stable sorts; single-threaded; garbage collected
  - point: 7
    score: 2
    evidence: memory-safe without unsafe; a panic exits 2 where the original exits 1, so the top must recover
  - point: 8
    score: 1
    evidence: the type checker and go vet check little of what the fabulac states; the judge is the check
  - point: 9
    score: 2
    evidence: not measured at the weighing (no run); provisional; measure at A8 and O9
  - point: 10
    score: 2
    evidence: no budget stated; 30 seconds a step allowed; to be timed at O8
  - point: 11
    score: 2
    evidence: plain Go, about 4,000 to 5,000 lines
  - point: 12
    score: 3
    evidence: no framework, two small modules; the fabulac stays the source
  provides:
  - for: C:reliance/V-R01
    by: built-in
    what: path/filepath
  - for: C:reliance/V-R02
    by: written
    what: tokenizer and recursive-descent parser of the 3.13 grammar
    note: the riskiest use; spike told/go-spike
  - for: C:reliance/V-R03
    by: written
    what: an option reader with prefixes of long options
    note: help free and usage errors alike for Go
  - for: C:reliance/V-R04
    by: built-in
    what: strconv
    note: free for Go
  - for: C:reliance/V-R05
    by: written
    what: case-insensitive glob
    note: ruled changed
  - for: C:reliance/V-R06
    by: written
    what: glob where * matches any run including /
  - for: C:reliance/V-R07
    by: written
    what: the same glob, case-sensitive; decorator names
  - for: C:reliance/V-R08
    by: library
    what: a TOML 1.0 module pinned in go.mod and go.sum
    note: X0_FETCH=1 at build; sitting 1 Q3
  - for: C:reliance/V-R09
    by: written
    what: a check of the decoded value's kind with the original's kind names
  - for: C:reliance/V-R10
    by: written
    what: constant folding on the tree
  - for: C:reliance/V-R11
    by: written
    what: reachability examining every handler
    note: ruled changed
  - for: C:reliance/V-R12
    by: written
    what: reachability
  - for: C:reliance/V-R13
    by: written
    what: a map keyed by file, first line and name
  - for: C:reliance/V-R14
    by: library
    what: sort.SliceStable with full lower-casing from golang.org/x/text/cases
    note: ties free for Go
  - for: C:reliance/V-R15
    by: built-in
    what: filepath.WalkDir and filepath.EvalSymlinks
    note: linked files changed; order free
  - for: C:reliance/V-R16
    by: written
    what: a noqa scanner
  - for: C:reliance/V-R17
    by: written
    what: trimming with the white-space set plus U+001C to U+001F
  - for: C:reliance/V-R18
    by: built-in
    what: splitting at \n only
    note: ruled changed
  - for: C:reliance/V-R19
    by: library
    what: golang.org/x/text/unicode/norm NFKC
    note: Unicode table version against 15.1.0
  - for: C:reliance/V-R20
    by: built-in
    what: unicode.IsLetter and unicode.IsNumber
  - for: C:reliance/V-R21
    by: written
    what: the brace format-field reader
  - for: C:reliance/V-R22
    by: written
    what: recover at the top and exit 1
  - for: C:reliance/V-R23
    by: built-in
    what: fmt.Fprintln to standard error and os.Exit(1)
  - for: C:reliance/V-R24
    by: written
    what: UTF-8 with or without BOM, latin-1 and a cp1252 table, the coding cookie
    note: other codecs free for Go
  - for: C:reliance/V-R25
    by: written
    what: the read-error message with empty text
  - for: C:reliance/V-R26
    by: written
    what: the parser's own messages
    note: alike stderr-said-or-not
  - for: C:reliance/V-R27
    by: written
    what: type comments parsed alone and walked; a bad one stops the walk
    note: kept-wrong; part of the riskiest use
  - for: C:reliance/V-R28
    by: built-in
    what: embed of the whitelist files, scanned by the same parser
  - for: C:reliance/V-R29
    by: built-in
    what: os.Stat
  - for: C:reliance/V-R30
    by: dropped
    what: any dump
    note: free for Go
  - for: C:reliance/V-R31
    by: built-in
    what: filepath.Rel and filepath.EvalSymlinks
  - for: C:reliance/V-R32
    by: built-in
    what: UTF-8 bytes written as they are
    note: the b'...' fallback free
  - for: C:reliance/V-R33
    by: built-in
    what: os.Exit
  spike:
    use: the 3.13 grammar with type comments (C:reliance/V-R02, C:reliance/V-R27) on P:case/x0.V-C32 and P:case/x0.V-C33
    level: 3
    where: _x0/vulture/told/go-spike/
    judged-by: O8 (x0.sh build and judge, label go-spike)
    evidence:
      level: 3
      against: original
      cases:
      - P:case/x0.V-C32
      - P:case/x0.V-C33
      differ:
        ruled: 0
        unruled: 0
      where:
        file: ../results/2026-11-18-1819/vulture/go-spike/verdict.json
        digest: 8a7e5ccb04cfb214ce81088367228c5d011de67c7b458620158f610cd3ed4c6e
      at: 2026-11-18T18:19
  verdict: feasible-with
  conditions:
  - the written parser agrees on V-C32 and V-C33 at O8 (spike level 2 or better on its cases)
  - a TOML 1.0 module and golang.org/x/text are pinned in go.sum at A8 and built with X0_FETCH=1
  - the option reader is written (prefixes of long options, exit 2)
  - uncaught errors exit 1
  at: '2026-11-18'
  by: R:maker/agent-w1-xp
  made:
    move: weigh
    in: go
    by-hand: true
    step: A7
    run: x0-A7-2026-11-18
    engine: model:claude-opus-5-5
  provenance:
    mode: manual
    confidence: 1
    sources:
    - _x0/vulture/vulture.fabulac.cosm
    - _x0/sitting-1.md
    - _x0/vulture/rulings.json
    - orangepaper "Transcoding through the fabulac", tab The paper, "Choosing the target"
    state: known
